  "narrative": "The new evidence is highly favorable to the SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 association and generally reassuring for specificity. H44 shows a very large non-Avana-library effect: R28 is +0.801 signed, interval +0.748 to +0.853, with valid cell sizes 61 and 174. Because H44's direction is -1, this corresponds to a strongly negative raw exposed-minus-comparator difference, i.e. much stronger SMARCA2 dependency in SMARCA4-loss tumors outside the dominant Avana stratum. This is far above the 10% relative benchmark and much larger than any observed control effect. H36 is similarly informative: R35 is +0.777 signed, interval +0.756 to +0.798, in ARID1A-wild-type tumors. This supports the specificity of SMARCA4 loss rather than generic BAF-complex loss, and H37 is null: R36 is -0.003, interval -0.025 to +0.019, arguing against ARID1A loss independently predicting stronger SMARCA2 dependency in SMARCA4-wild-type tumors. H46, H51, and H52 are marker controls; R30, R33, and R34 are all near null and far from the large biomarker effects, which reduces concern that these very large associations are driven by nonspecific role-free marker association. H45 confirms that the validated KEAP1/NFE2L2 reversal is also large in non-Avana samples: R29 is +0.794, interval +0.746 to +0.842.\n\nThe WRN robustness picture is less complete. H43 failed because the non-Avana MSI-high exposed cell had only 10 observations, so it provides no usable evidence and remains unresolved/deferred. H49 WRN batch_a interaction is not decisive: R31 is +0.048 signed, interval -0.019 to +0.115. Directionally it is compatible with a somewhat stronger association in batch_a, but the interval includes zero and admits both small and clinically large effects, so it cannot close the technical question. H50 for SMARCA2 is statistically significant but in the opposite direction to the hypothesized signed claim: R32 is -0.051 signed, interval -0.095 to -0.007. This corresponds to a modestly weaker raw association in batch_a relative to its complement. I reject the specific H50 direction, but I keep it active as a small technical caveat because the interval is not negligible and it is the one result suggesting possible screen-batch heterogeneity for SMARCA2. The main effect is so large, and the non-Avana and ARID1A-wild-type estimates are so consistent, that this small opposite interaction does not currently outweigh the association; however, I registered batch-specific main-effect proposals to quantify whether the SMARCA4 effect remains large within batch_a itself.\n\nThe EGFR signal remains unresolved. H53 is directionally supportive of stronger EGFR dependency with EGFR amplification in TP53-loss tumors (R37 +0.025, interval -0.031 to +0.080), but the point estimate is borderline relative to the 10% benchmark and the interval is wide because of smaller cells. H54 STK11 loss is null for KRAS dependency. Given that H7 now has enormous main discovery evidence, Avana robustness, non-Avana robustness, ARID1A-specificity, and null marker controls, I request independent validation of H7 rather than H6. H6 remains active, but its non-Avana stratum could not be estimated and its batch interaction remains underpowered; H7 is currently the most mature unvalidated large association. The request is an independent replication of an association in this dataset, not a test of causality or generalizability beyond the supplied system.",
  "research_notes": "Evidence state after iteration 3 appraisal. Independently validated accepted associations: H11 TP53 loss -> much weaker USP7 dependency; H17 KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Large but not yet independently validated: H6 MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency; H7 SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency. New iteration-3 evidence strongly supports H7 robustness: H44 non-Avana +0.8009 [0.7485,0.8534]; H36 ARID1A-wild-type +0.7770 [0.7558,0.7983]; H46 marker-E control null +0.0061 [-0.0260,0.0383]; H52 marker-F control null +0.0153 [-0.0168,0.0474]. H37 ARID1A loss in SMARCA4-wt is null -0.0031 [-0.0252,0.0190]. H45 non-Avana NFE2L2 reversal accepts +0.7939 [0.7457,0.8422]. WRN robustness remains less complete: H43 non-Avana invalid due exposed n=10; H49 batch interaction inconclusive +0.0476 [-0.0195,0.1146]; H51 marker-F control null -0.0072 [-0.0303,0.0159]. Technical caveat: H50 SMARCA2 batch_a interaction is small opposite to hypothesized direction -0.0509 [-0.0950,-0.0069], not supportive of H50 but worth quantifying with batch_a main effect. Validation requested: H7. If validation is concordant, accept H7 with independent evidence while retaining the batch interaction as a small within-dataset caveat. If validation is discordant, revise H7 and prioritize technical confounding or cohort-structure explanations.\n\nPending informative items: H56 SMARCA4 loss in ARID1A-loss tumors; H42 USP7 marker-E control; H47 NFE2L2 marker-E control; H55 STAT3 with PTEN loss; EGFR refinements H30, H38, H48, H53; KRAS subtype/co-mutation items H13, H39, H40; broad outcome/marker items H21, H22. Proposed next analyses: batch_a main effects for WRN and SMARCA2 to interpret batch interactions. Next allocation should run H7 validation response, H56, H42, H47, H55, and batch main effects if enough slots remain. EGFR should be downgraded if co-mutation strata remain small and below clinical significance; do not accept unless a refined stratum shows robust clinically significant difference.",
